-- BUILT (unit SRM20): dev runs a1–a7 (a1–a6 exit 1, a7 exit 0); the final-SHA rebuild in REPORT-SRM20.md is the only final evidence.
-- SCOPE (SRM20 audits) of `topshare{M,Q}_svBoundsH_underComposedG`.  (1) PREMISE TABLE (index, binderInfo, name, Prop-or-data, type) equal to `Tests/Compiler/Srm20AuditExpected.lean` and `scripts/srm20/PREMISES.txt`, `S20THM` marker per theorem, literal count guard;
-- three semantic negative fixtures (` ∧ True` on a Prop binder, added data binder, reordered binders), each non-vacuous and rejected.  REGENERATION: build Tests.Compiler.Srm20AuditTest, then `python3 scripts/srm20/gen_audit.py LOG`.
-- (2) INDEPENDENT FULL-TYPE EXPECTED STATEMENTS: `Tests/Compiler/Srm20ExpStmt.lean` GENERATED by scripts/srm20/gen_exp.py from the SOURCE statements of SRM9 `topshare*_hierC_at_free` (which consumes the ComposedG statement) and SRM19 `topshare*_svBoundsH_endToEnd`
-- through the committed substitution list, and the text of `QDepthLift` from scripts/srm20/EXPECTED.txt (fixed before proving); `isDefEq` to each final type; three wrong expected forms (hfit deleted; Reset hypothesis dropped; hlift binder dropped) are rejected.
-- (3) ONE WITNESS: one RunsTo/hcore/hpost/raw/b/D binder, no `hrun` binder; in the conclusion the ComposedG witnesses ids/cache/regs occur in the hypotheses, and the run, the SVBoundsH conclusion share the seed, T, start state and `envs`.
-- (4) QDepthLift is not defeq to any other Prop binder of its theorem; the depth-2 (SRM9 ComposedG) vs depth-1 (SRM19) difference of topshareQ is asserted on the two source statements.
-- (5) CLOSURE: standard axioms; forbidden old-form roots (with control); ComposedG, composedG_of_NW, SRM9 `topshare*_composed_binder` and `_hierC_at_free`, machine_ships_hierC_at_free AND the SRM19 endToEnd are in each theorem's closure.
set_option Elab.async false
